course: dictionary
lesson: 4244
title: Granny and her family words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A granny is your grandmother, the mother of your mum or dad. «Granny» is a warm, friendly word, and it tells the reader that the speaker is a child or is close to the old lady. «Gracie runs in and calls Granny «Mammy» by accident» shows that Gracie is so close to her granny that she nearly used the word for her own mum.
explain: Granny has other names too: gran, grandma and nan all mean the same thing. Read the words around a word to find which one fits. «Stay with Granny» and «Granny's house» are both about a family home, so the clues tell you the word means someone you love and visit.
explain: Granny also turns up in phrases where it is not about a person. A «granny flat» is a small home for an older relative, next to the family house. A «granny knot» is a weak, wrong reef knot, and a «granny smith» is a green apple. Always check the whole phrase, not just the word granny.
fact: Granny means your grandmother, the mother of your mum or dad.
fact: Gran, grandma and nan are other words that mean the same as granny.
fact: A granny flat is a small home for an older relative, next to the family house.
fact: A granny knot is a weak, wrong reef knot.
fact: A granny smith is a green apple.
fact: «Chī le ma?» means «have you eaten?» Grandparents and neighbours use it as a greeting, and the polite answer is «chī le», which means «I have».
exercise: Gracie runs in and calls Granny «Mammy» by accident. What is Granny in this story? | A friend from school | A shopkeeper | A teacher at her school | *Her grandmother, the mother of her mum or dad
exercise: Ella hears about a «granny flat» next to the family house. What is a granny flat? | A flat with a garden just for pets | *A small home for an older relative next to the family house | A flat in a block with a lift | A shop that sells cakes
exercise: «Answer «no» and a granny may well start cooking for you.» Find and copy one word that means the same as granny. | answer | *nan | start | cooking
test: What is a «granny smith»? | A red sweet | A kind of grandma's shoe | *A green apple | A type of car
test: «Chī le ma?» is a greeting used by grandparents and neighbours. What does it mean? | Where do you live? | Goodbye, see you later | What is your name? | *Have you eaten?
exam: What does «granny knot» describe? | A kind of cake baked at home | *A weak, wrong reef knot | A bow for tying a shoe | A tight, strong knot used for climbing
